config CRAM
	tristate "Compressed-RAM private-node read-only tier"
	depends on NUMA && MIGRATION && MMU && MEMORY_HOTPLUG
	select BALLOON
	help
	  Manage folios demoted onto private memory nodes (e.g. compressed
	  CXL memory) as a read-only tier.  Folios are diverted onto a CRAM
	  private node during reclaim and mapped present read-only so reads
	  are zero-copy; write faults promote the folio back to DRAM.  Entry
	  is by migration (no swap dependency).

	  A device driver registers its memory with cram_register(); the
	  write fence itself is core mm and needs nothing from here.

	  If unsure, say N.
